# WAFscan – XSS Sample Tests

## Overview

This directory contains a demonstration of WAFscan's signature-based XSS testing approach.

## Components

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| xss-signatures.txt | Sample XSS test definitions |
| xss_test_runner.py | Python HTTP test runner |
| results/ | Test execution results |

## Test methodology

1. Load test definitions.
2. Extract test ID and test marker.
3. Submit each test to the designated HTTP parameter.
4. Record HTTP response status.
5. Check whether the original marker is reflected.
6. Export results to CSV.

## Limitations

This is a basic demonstration, not a complete XSS vulnerability scanner or WAF effectiveness assessment.

HTTP response status and marker reflection are observations only. They do not independently establish whether a WAF successfully blocked an attack or whether an application is vulnerable.

Use only authorized local test environments.

